      "url": "https://gadamer-ojs-tamu.tdl.org/gadamer/issue/view/1",
      "description": "<p data-start=\"324\" data-end=\"556\">This is the inaugural issue of <em data-start=\"357\" data-end=\"389\">The Journal of Gadamer Studies</em>. Volume 1, issue 1 features a newly translated essay by Gadamer on the poet Hilde Domin as well as articles exploring themes such as the hermeneutics of prayer, Gadamer’s philosophy of art, metaphysical hermeneutics, the immediacy of experience, and Gadamer’s dialogue with Parmenides. Also included is a book symposium on <em data-start=\"938\" data-end=\"986\">The Event of Meaning in Gadamer’s Hermeneutics</em> and a review of <em data-start=\"1007\" data-end=\"1052\">Gadamer and the Social Turn in Epistemology</em>.</p>"
    },
